Transcribed from the authors' output screenshot,
reference/Plots/ergm_choice6_star_estimation_result.PNG, which reports
MCMLE.maxit = 200. It is the only place these numbers exist -- the authors
published an image, not a table -- so unlike every other file in this
directory it was typed rather than written by a script, and cannot be
regenerated without re-running their fit.

results/r/mcmle_star.csv holds this repo's own run at the same setting. The
two agree to within 0.12 standard errors on every term, which is what two
Monte Carlo runs give -- but they differ at the third significant figure
(1.6014 against 1.5983 on b2cov.V3), so do not expect them to match digit for
digit.
